{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:31:47.189246Z","id":"86ca4f33cf4d55b54fdbf9ca060227b905b4d44441908b81601527d484ff4993","body":{"detail":"The same holds for Toolbox.stopAtCap without a cap handler. A cut-off or invalid turn is counted by RunBudget.addTurn (it was paid for), so its resend counts against the turn cap too.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"1a93f0902d8e160286df463133e031fefec3717da95ce16a458bad6b90151f9d"},"summary":"A refusal or a second cut-off turn ends the run with a RunGaveUp set by the runner, not by give_up: nothing is replied on the threads, so AgentLoop and FeedbackWorker must reply 'Couldn't make that change: <reason>' for a runner-made RunGaveUp (answered: false)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:31:47.189279Z","id":"8f5fec9f7a5d3e88aac86f8d7dafe7b21809dfcd27d18108073c981d732697a3","body":{"detail":"The runner sends a broken turn (ModelTurn.broken: a tool call's input_json_delta text does not parse as an object) again once, unchanged, and gives up on a second. Answering in place would keep the turn but must echo an assistant tool_use with an input the model never wrote; resending keeps the history exactly what the model produced.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"5660f071f20a28a0582149d402c01936ac0eb413fa6bdc836434067b737b1fd9"},"summary":"Answer a tool call whose streamed input is not JSON with an INVALID_JSON error tool_result instead of sending the turn again","tags":["revisit:live runs show invalid eager tool input more than rarely","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:50:45.146698Z","id":"97c8c47b34a4e2828bff972614f21905255ec4a93876fa4bf4febe85b43a1f5c","body":{"detail":"With server-side fallbacks, a decline after output began keeps the partial in the same stream, marks the switch with a content block of type 'fallback', and the fallback model continues; only the partial's text blocks were the fallback model's context. The API's echo rule: omit thinking, redacted_thinking and tool_use blocks that appear before the last 'fallback' block. Today MessageStream.message (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/message_stream.dart) rebuilds every block, so: (a) a declined tool_use whose input happened to be whole is run by the loop (lines 175-196) and answered, though the serving model never made that call; (b) a declined tool_use cut mid-input throws InvalidToolInput, so the turn comes back broken (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart, turn's onOk) and the fallback model's good answer is thrown away and paid for again; (c) the declined thinking blocks are echoed. Also, top-level usage covers only the serving attempt (usage.iterations holds each attempt) and the served model (message 'model') may differ from the requested one, so RunBudget.addTurn under-counts the cost cap after a mid-stream decline. Rare in practice (the 5.5 classifiers decline cyber, bio, frontier_llm, reasoning_extraction, general_harms), and no test streams a 'fallback' block.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"722e16bffba0eae390eacaad7b83ad9f6b0ce7486013ac2d6a151b2d7bfdf082"},"suggested_fix":"In the turn's onOk (or MessageStream), find the last 'fallback' block and drop thinking/redacted_thinking/tool_use blocks before it (and judge InvalidToolInput only after it); price from usage.iterations when present. Test: a streamed turn with a partial write_file, a fallback block, then a whole write_file and finish runs only the second and echoes no block before the boundary except text.","summary":"A mid-stream fallback (fallbacks 'default' on sonnet/opus 5.5) leaves the declined attempt's thinking and tool_use blocks before the fallback block: the runner echoes them and runs a whole declined tool_use, and a cut-off declined tool_use breaks the whole turn","tags":["review","fallbacks","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:50:45.146741Z","id":"012e16054bd3511210f90fb052264832566090649e39f9dd184ddff53ea13c78","body":{"detail":"RunBudget.addTurn counts the cut turn's output before the loop's top re-checks hardStop (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/budget.dart, hardStop: _usage.output >= caps.outputTokens), so the resend branch only runs when the cut turn reported fewer output tokens than the cap. The tests in group truncated_write_never_reaches_the_draft (apps/clax_app/test/agent/runner/messages_runner_test.dart:264-358) pass only because streamedTurn (apps/clax_app/test/support/fake_messages_api.dart:362) reports output_tokens 1 for a max_tokens stop, which a real cut never does. The user-facing result is still safe (stopAtCap publishes the last clean draft or gives up naming the output cap), but the test pins a path production never takes and nothing pins the path it does take. The resend's value itself is fine: 64000 is within claude-haiku-5-5's 128K output limit (and the 5.5 Sonnet/Opus limits).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":166},"content_hash":"c50a9ab4fe716d1ff83ad83830db735cb4b76178892da33bc930bde0c27947b6"},"suggested_fix":"Give the cut turn a realistic usage (output_tokens 32000) in one test and expect the cap stop ('20000 output tokens') with the draft untouched; then either drop the resend for max_tokens (keep it for the broken-JSON case) or size the per-turn max_tokens from the remaining output cap. The plan or spec owner chooses which.","summary":"The max_tokens resend at 64000 cannot happen under the R§4.4 caps: a turn cut at max_tokens 32000 has spent at least the change cap (20,000) or the new-app cap (32,000), so the next loop pass stops at the output-token cap instead","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:50:45.146805Z","id":"f8915e47d697d26d7092cea626ea1c247f0caf9140d0058c628cab7c8e53bf2a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"86ca4f33cf4d55b54fdbf9ca060227b905b4d44441908b81601527d484ff4993","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"9f19b30e01d3a7736dd29142bdea3915e81a9eb50395eec4b73486af66f86e28"},"summary":"The same runner-made endings (RunCancelled between turns at lines 114/136/193/201, a refusal, a second cut) also never reach RenderTool.cleanup (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart:158), so a draft artifact created by an earlier render is left until the daemon's one-hour sweep; whoever owns the run's end (A7's AgentLoop/FeedbackWorker) must call cleanup for every outcome, not only finish/give_up/capStop.","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:57:32.602270Z","id":"56cddcff413923d34d87b505ae5ab4b87c4526a640f79c3ee799a8cceeea98e6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e4182d52","summary":"Fixed in e4182d52: MessagesApiBackend.turn rebuilds the turn with MessageStream.echoMessage (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/message_stream.dart), which before the last fallback block keeps only text, fallback and paired server tool blocks and judges JSON input only for kept blocks; a fallback block's start emits AttemptStarted so the preview drops the declined partial; usage is summed over usage.iterations and RunBudget.addTurn prices each attempt at its model (a fallback_message at the fallback block's to.model, else the message's model). Tests 'mid-output fallback runs only the serving model's calls and echoes none of the declined attempt but its text' (a whole declined delete_file and a cut declined write_file before the boundary: neither runs, the turn is not broken, the echo is [text, fallback, served thinking, served write]) and 'mid-output fallback each attempt is counted, at the price of the model that ran it'; both fail with stream.message in place of stream.echoMessage. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/agent/runner/messages_runner_test.dart: +34, All tests passed; flutter test test/agent: +408 ~1, All tests passed.","supersedes":"97c8c47b34a4e2828bff972614f21905255ec4a93876fa4bf4febe85b43a1f5c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:57:32.602864Z","id":"52d4cc21209afe2fcfb310b97fd426ac11fda0555c1c9d02cef4589b8969f6b6","body":{"detail":"The output cap (R§4.4: 20,000 / 32,000) already bounds what a run may write, so a turn larger than what is left can only end at the cap anyway; sizing max_tokens to it makes a max_tokens stop mean 'the cap is spent', which goes straight to Toolbox.stopAtCap (last clean draft or give up) instead of a resend path production could never reach. A cut-off turn still never runs its tools. Only when caps above 32000 leave output after a cut is the turn sent once more, sized to what is left; a broken-JSON turn is still sent once more.","kind":"comment","references":"012e16054bd3511210f90fb052264832566090649e39f9dd184ddff53ea13c78","summary":"Decided (a technical call, not an owner decision): each turn's max_tokens is the run's output cap left, at most 32000, and the 64000 resend is dropped.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:57:32.602902Z","id":"e9c705cb07636d0415446a054decd74cb1f4f9d01c4348d060b9de8b74e01648","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e4182d52","summary":"Fixed in e4182d52: _Run._maxTokens sends min(32000, caps.outputTokens - usage.output) and a max_tokens stop with the cap spent returns Toolbox.stopAtCap; streamedTurn (apps/clax_app/test/support/fake_messages_api.dart) reports 20000 output tokens for a max_tokens stop by default. Tests in group truncated_write_never_reaches_the_draft: 'a turn cut at the output cap stops at the cap; the draft never sees the cut write' (one request at max_tokens 20000, RunGaveUp('20000 output tokens'), draft revision 0), 'a turn cut at the cap after a clean render publishes that render', 'a cut with output cap left is sent again, sized to what is left, without its partial output' (40000 cap: 32000 then 8000), and 'max_tokens is the output cap left, at most 32000'. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/agent/runner/messages_runner_test.dart: +34, All tests passed; flutter test test/agent: +408 ~1, All tests passed.","supersedes":"012e16054bd3511210f90fb052264832566090649e39f9dd184ddff53ea13c78","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:57:32.603486Z","id":"691f40a861b5f66a252861a0582102d963dea45797f661ff26d8ac0fd959bc5f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f8915e47d697d26d7092cea626ea1c247f0caf9140d0058c628cab7c8e53bf2a","summary":"Confirmed as the contract: MessagesApiRunner.run returns RunCancelled, a refusal's RunGaveUp and a broken turn's RunGaveUp without calling any tool, so it neither replies nor deletes the draft artifact; the owner of the run's end (AgentLoop/FeedbackWorker, Task A7) calls RenderTool.cleanup and replies for every outcome, not only after finish, give_up or capStop. Since e4182d52 a cut-off turn normally ends at the output cap through stopAtCap; a second cut gives up only under caps above 32000.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.801292Z","id":"7f01fb03e3cc33fd15fc0df8a352287fdb1773f31a197cd3b644374ffca22eb3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7de1c0e9","summary":"Fixed in 7de1c0e9: AgentLoop (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart, _runTools and _changeTools) calls RenderTool.cleanup on every end, the runner's own included, and replies failureReply(<reason>) on the threads, skipping ones with a newer comment, then acknowledges, for a RunGaveUp the runner made and for a model failure. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart: 'a refusal the runner ends the run on gets the failure reply, the comment acknowledged and the draft deleted', 'a model failure gets the failure reply with its message', 'a runner-made ending skips a thread the person wrote on again', and for a new app 'a refusal the runner ends the run on throws, and deletes the draft its earlier render made'. flutter test test/agent test/app_background_test.dart test/app_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart: +623, all passed.","supersedes":"86ca4f33cf4d55b54fdbf9ca060227b905b4d44441908b81601527d484ff4993","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:56:43.004242Z","id":"290d378bb2e17d2485665a960ee6ddd69c4d4d23a9970d76ed237f53f71da382","body":{"detail":"Failure: a run whose connection keeps breaking mid-answer (stream sends events, then a network cut in front) reaches caps.turns or caps.costUsd through TurnHolds.onCutAttempt (messages_runner.dart:98, state.budget.addTurn). RunBudget.hardStop is read only at the top of _loop (messages_runner.dart:144), after backend.turn returns, and ResumingTurns.turn (lib/platform/network_pause.dart:240-296) loops without consulting it. So the turn is sent again up to maxOfflineResends (5) more times after every ApiConnection.nudge (each Try now, each return of the app to the front), each billed, while the budget already reads over its cap; only the wall-clock cap can end it, and it counts only the time spent streaming (the holds pause it). The turn and cost caps bound nothing until an attempt finally completes.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":89},"end":{"line":99},"content_hash":"219420b15b79e52ed7353ead12492cc720e5f789f2b2076029ec784ada4ccea2"},"suggested_fix":"In onCutAttempt, after addTurn, stop the run when a cap is reached: `if (state.budget.hardStop != null) _fire(_Stop.timeUp)` (or a new _Stop.capped). The hold's cancel (r.cancelled = _stop.future) then throws AgentError.cancelled and _loop returns _cap(hardStop) at messages_runner.dart:167-168. Test: a stub TurnBackend that cuts after an event with caps.turns = 2 ends the run capped, with no attempt after the cap.","summary":"Cut attempts are counted toward the run's caps but never stop the run: a turn keeps resending past hardStop","tags":["review","risk:cost","offline","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:56:43.004428Z","id":"f8183d04081f644ac097c4d34d8a5808c4d0856e95b3642c5fe076d29c6020d7","body":{"detail":"_sentBefore starts as const Usage() and is set only after a turn completes (messages_runner.dart:171-175), so onCutAttempt (line 98) adds a zero-usage turn for every cut of the first turn, whose input (system prompt, tools, first message) is the largest uncached send of the run. Output streamed before any cut is never counted either, so caps.outputTokens and caps.costUsd undercount a run on a breaking connection. The waiver 9ca0b154 on lib/platform/network_pause.dart:154-180 ('a turn attempt cut by the network is never priced') no longer matches the code since onCutAttempt and wants restating.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"0825718790da2812c201b856430f2e522d962be2f08476f125683277bef61682"},"suggested_fix":"Seed _sentBefore with an estimate of the first request's input (or count the first cut at the turn's maxTokens-free input estimate), and have the backend report partial usage from the stream's message_start/message_delta events on a cut.","summary":"A cut attempt of the run's first turn is counted at no cost, and no cut attempt counts the output it streamed","tags":["review","risk:cost","offline","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:02:33.872994Z","id":"66e918483120c92a6e98f5e99bb6fa7b758674fcf498bac6abbd428f82931e49","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f066a64e","summary":"_Run._cutAttempt now fires _Stop.capped when the counted cut reaches a hard cap, so the held turn's hold is cancelled and _loop returns _cap(hardStop). Evidence: test/platform/network_pause_test.dart 'each cut attempt that reached the API is priced, the first turn's too, and a cap it reaches ends the run without sending the turn again' (caps.turns 2, a backend that cuts after an event: 2 sends, RunGaveUp '2 turns') passes; flutter test of network_pause_test, worker_offline_test, test/agent/runner, connection_test: +83 passed.","supersedes":"290d378bb2e17d2485665a960ee6ddd69c4d4d23a9970d76ed237f53f71da382","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:02:33.888995Z","id":"fcf02f7165373e01d6514c4042d6beee1bd266608cae02342b4e37af1f764cca","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f066a64e","summary":"A cut attempt is priced as the last turn's input plus the history added since (about 4 characters a token; the whole request on the first turn) and MessagesApiRunner.tokensPerEvent (10) output tokens per server-sent event it streamed. Evidence: the same test asserts costUsd > 0 on first-turn cuts and usage.output == 2 * tokensPerEvent; passes.","supersedes":"f8183d04081f644ac097c4d34d8a5808c4d0856e95b3642c5fe076d29c6020d7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
